<%= header_section("Weekly payout batch slice failed") %>
<div>
  <p><code>PerformPayoutsForUserSliceWorker</code> exhausted Sidekiq retries for one slice of this week's run. The rest of the batch is unaffected — only the sellers in this slice have NOT had payouts created.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Processor: <%= @payout_processor_type %></li>
    <li>Bank account type: <%= @bank_account_type.presence || "(none — this is the Friday run)" %></li>
    <li>Sellers in this slice: <%= @seller_count || "unknown" %></li>
    <li>Error: <%= @error_class %>: <%= @error_message %></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Retry the dead job itself from the Sidekiq dead set once the underlying issue is resolved — it carries the exact seller ids for this slice, and re-running it is safe because sellers whose payouts were already created are skipped. Do NOT re-run <code>PerformPayoutsUpToDelayDaysAgoWorker</code> for this: that re-walks the whole processor bucket and writes duplicate payout notes for every seller who isn't eligible.</p>
  <p>See Sentry for the full backtrace. Verify recovery by checking that the sellers in the slice have a <code>payments</code> row for this payout period.</p>
</div>
